+# Manual fold overlay — Site handoff for repository main
+
+Base Site commit: d4155931cd760d4222c9f66916551110eb40053b (version14). Integration target: research repository main, through the repository owner. This task did not modify or push the research checkout.
+
+Pinned research source: e75ecbbba1c0913d98f51a5b8ac23192dac9723e. Read the exact MONUMENT-SLIDE-OVERLAY-SPEC, MONUMENT-SLIDE-REGISTRATION-AMENDMENT and MONUMENT-FOLD-SLIDE-FINDINGS. Extracted input/glyphs from the supplied fold-slide-020.html; SHA256 8aa6e64f92260302c66a279bae1420180d28b7b335734a910b528d089582949a. Runtime data is unchanged. The134 offline records are a separate test oracle, not a row-shift significance model.
+
+New fourth mode has signed column offsets −33…+33 and row offsets −28…+28, accessible one-cell buttons and integer sliders, reset to anchored primary full overlap, inspection fields/click, source coordinates, exact A–Z highlights, counts/denominators, approximate common-aperture display, and JSON export of inputs/offsets/current matches. There is no wrapping. Outside is excluded from two-layer overlap; padding is solid; question marks are not label wildcards. MYVGT/AABCD is reproduced at model column2 with headerA then keyA/B/C/D; first cipherE protrudes. Two reflections cancel the column-order reversal and glyph handedness reversal. Row order is preserved before any explicit exploratory row translation. Source columns exclude automatic centering padding while preserving literal header blanks. The retained DUNIN_HEADER33 sensitivity input has one literal leading header blank before additional centering; the resulting grid has two leading blanks.
+
+Exact labels and approximate aperture AND are separate. Pixel glyphs are the same pinned5×7 square-aperture dictionary, not measured copper outlines. Flat coincident equal-scale/baseline sheets and normal rays are an explicitly separate surrogate, not the existing courtyard Sun/thickness/curvature solver. Current manual matched letters are descriptive ciphertext coincidences, not a plaintext extraction. Prior systematic work was column-only at row0; all nonzero row shifts are visibly exploratory. No inherited p-values are used.
+
+Tests cover all134 canonical column frames and every numerical endpoint, anchor mask intersections12/2/7/13/5, both reflections, every original row/mask, repeated one-cell buttons, bounds and empty overlap, row+column composition, source coordinates, punctuation, K4 match positions14/44/72/95, invalid integer atomic restore, reset and JSON match export. Full suite87 tests passed. Existing optical kernels, K1–K3 module, entrance drawing, confirmed-only K4 clues and238 frozen validation files are unchanged.
+
+Supported native-browser QA was attempted in thisMac executor: cua.getState returned no apps/browsers and explicitly reported theMac locked. No unlock workaround or alternate browser environment was attempted. Actual rendered layout, pointer and native keyboard QA remain blocked. The supplied qa/fold-overlay.html runs the complete Site in390px and1280px frames, checks unit steps/reset/empty overlap/aperture display/scrolling/mode transitions/state preservation and overflow; it is not claimed to have run. DOM-control tests passed. No real-device/touch verification is claimed.
+
+Runtime: candidate/ and dist/ app.mjs,index.html,style.css; new fold-overlay/ modules and pinned protocol files; root release manifest. Tests: tests/fold-overlay.test.mjs and fold-offline-records.json. Preview: serve repository root and open qa/fold-overlay.html. No new runtime dependencies or paid services. Existing public audience is preserved. Dedicated fold JSON export preserves the complete fold inputs and matched source positions; the global optical export includes fold state only as supplementary UI metadata.
