+# FOLD-SLIDE-020 — amended progressive two-layer comparison
+
+23 October 2026. USER STEERING BEFORE ANY MATCH SCORING supersedes the static-only FOLD-OVERLAY-020 protocol at0079ed2. The old static ciphertext-self axes and printed-face control are deferred/unrun; they are not counted as tested. The intended halves are the front-readable ciphertext region and back-readable tableau region. CIA's description independently confirms that opposite-face orientation. The complete source rows and geometry limitations remain those pinned in the earlier input.
+
+Explicit transforms: initial tableau view reverses BOTH column order and glyph handedness in the common cipher-front frame; folding across the central vertical seam reverses BOTH again. The intended full-overlap state therefore compares same-row/same-column, SAME-FACING glyphs. Do not leave a spurious glyph reflection. The two separately readable transcripts are the post-double-reflection reference. Subsequent translation changes horizontal position only.
+
+Use exactly the earlier LITERAL and CENTER33 registrations, no fitted offsets. Fixed ciphertext occupies columns0..32; folded tableau occupies columns s..s+32. Positive s moves tableau right, negative s left; compare C[r,c] with T[r,c-s] only when BOTH sheets cover that cell. No wrapping. Enumerate every integer s=-33..33:134 frames across two registrations, with zero represented once per registration. Display scans0,+1,..,+33 and0,-1,..,-33; the end frames have zero overlap. The separate halves of ciphertext interpretation is deferred after the user's clarification, not rejected.
+
+Symbolic identity: A–Z only, exact labels; punctuation/blanks/padding are not wildcards. Record all exact matches, source/target row and column, raw row index, full stream and K4 position. Reading order fixed ciphertext row-major. Matched strings are descriptive, not a decipherment or selected keyword.
+
+Approximate optical control: use the existing Site's original bridged5x7 square-aperture dictionary, copied read-only with pinned source commit/hash. This is a font surrogate, NOT measured copper glyphs. Preserve question-mark aperture; blanks/padding are solid copper. Assumed layers are flat, parallel/coincident, same scale and baseline, with normal orthographic rays. Every positive common square-pixel area transmits some modeled light; full coincidence requires equal nonempty masks. Distinct labels may transmit common area. No brightness threshold, grazing ray, thickness, shape calibration or metric pitch is inferred. No evidence permits physical light-through-monument claims.
+
+For each frame record geometric overlap cells=28*(33-|s|), comparable A–Z pairs, label matches, equal whole masks, nonempty common-aperture pairs, total common square-pixel area and common/union ink ratio. Include solid cells in the geometric denominator. Outside the common sheet rectangle is excluded from two-layer transmission; one-layer/edge escape is a different quantity. Zero-overlap frames have zero counts and undefined ratios, not division by zero or a match score. Keep continuous-light approximation and label identity separate.
+
+Null controls preserve fixed tableau, row length, punctuation, blank locations and the same complete shift/registration selector. Scheme A permutes A–Z independently within each original ciphertext row; Scheme B independently rotates each row's alphabetic sequence, retaining cyclic order/autocorrelation. Use1999 controls per scheme, seeds202610231230/202610231231. Each surrogate feeds ALL134 frames; no shift selection on actual data is retained for nulls. Active family has130 nonempty frames. Exact expected label/common-area totals come from per-row frequencies against each fixed tableau glyph, plus fixed punctuation contributions; these means hold under both schemes.
+
+Two endpoints only: label-match count and total common-aperture area. For each endpoint use fixed scaling (observed-exact_expected)/sqrt(max(expected,1)), only a comparison statistic, not a normal approximation. Compare every actual frame and actual family maximum with the complete null family maximum. Monte Carlo tails use(exceedances+1)/2000, never zero. Conservatively multiply by4 across two endpoints/two conditional-null reports; report schemes separately, not whichever looks better. Empty frames receive no p-value. K4 matches, matched strings and visual masks are descriptive outputs, not extra significance endpoints. No claim about artist intent, an English-language null or a cipher solution.
+
+Controls before actual scoring: independent row/column reflection/translation oracle; mirror twice restores every glyph/cell; same-facing identical glyphs coincide and different glyphs can overlap; zero/outside handling; source inventory/K4 indices; planted shift matches; independent per-pixel AND and exact expectation versus exhaustive tiny null enumeration; full-family seed replay and null structure invariants. Budget120 seconds per null scheme,1GiB RSS. Save every frame and null maxima, schematic offline visual, full results/tests/provenance and update existing hypothesis registry. No Site changes, extra shifts, alternate fonts or adaptive glyph/geometry tuning after outcomes.
