+# FOLD-SLIDE-020 — observed pole-edge registration, before scoring
+
+User's subsequent observation: nearest-pole vertical entries MYVGT and opposite AABCD. This amendment supersedes the earlier LITERAL/CENTER33 choice before any full-overlay match or null evaluation. It does not retune an observed high score: only the five directly supplied label pairs have been checked, all unequal.
+
+Read-only inspection of the existing Site source at d4155931 confirms both strings at centered-grid column1 (zero-based). Cipher row0 contributes raw character1=M; rows1–4 contribute raw character0=Y,V,G,T. Cipher E at row0/column0 protrudes one slot beyond this first full vertical glyph column. Tableau header contributes its first A, followed by the A/B/C/D row keys: no skipped header or shifted row. In the original common-front view, that readable tableau column1 is column31; initial view reflection and seam fold return it to cipher column1 with glyph handedness restored. Translation follows afterward. The pole/edge interpretation is tied to the stated render observation, not independently surveyed copper coordinates.
+
+Final models, exactly two: OBSERVED_RENDER33 is primary and reproduces both user strings; DUNIN_HEADER33 is a source-registration sensitivity retaining the two literal leading header blanks from Dunin HTML. All rows in BOTH models use the same33-column integer-centered convention. The rendered header is30 letters; the HTML header is blank+30 letters. Other characters, question marks, row breaks and extra L agree. Do not repair the extra L or silently shift any row. The old static self-fold axes, literal-left registration and printed-face control remain deferred/unrun.
+
+Continue exactly the earlier same-facing double-reflection model, offsets -33..33, no wrapping, all134 frames,130 active frames, optical surrogate and endpoints. Zero overlap has undefined ratios/no p-value. Fixed ciphertext coordinates determine reading order; opposite direction is the same offset family, not a second search counted at zero.
+
+Condition both null schemes on the five user-supplied cipher anchor characters at their ORIGINAL raw row indices. Preserve them exactly. Scheme A shuffles the remaining A–Z slots within each row; Scheme B rotates the remaining movable alphabetic sequence, preserving its cyclic order (not claiming preservation of the full row's autocorrelation across the fixed anchor). Punctuation/blanks remain fixed. Exact expectations use movable-slot frequencies plus each fixed anchor/question-mark contribution. Tableaux stay unchanged. Same1999 controls/seeds and all-shift selector; conservative factor4 correction across the two endpoints/two schemes remains. This conditioning charges the registration's known input rather than treating the supplied anchor as an untouched discovery.
+
+No further adjustment after scores. Approximate aperture AND is not identical-letter filtering and not measured physical light. A local offline visualization may show all shifts without Site changes/deployment.
