"true" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;pointer-events:none"></canvas></div><div class="scenefoot"><span>Drag to orbit · scroll / pinch to zoom</span><span><i class="copper"></i>Copper <i class="sun"></i>Direct sunlight</span></div><div id="selection" class="selection"></div></section></div><section class="lower"><div class="cipher"><div class="sectionhead">04 / RAW K4 · 97 CHARACTERS</div><p>Canonical K4 uses 31 columns, beginning at row 25, column 28. Full-screen mode preserves the complete cipher and tableau transcript lines (29–33 characters), at an assumed constant physical pitch. Its glyph shapes and spacing are unmeasured. Click a K4 letter to inspect its index.</p><p class="k4-clue-guide"><strong>Confirmed clues only</strong> · shown directly beneath each encrypted line. Mint letters are confirmed; neutral dots (·) are unknown. Positions count the first O as 1. This is not a solved message.</p><div id="letters"></div><div class="actions"><button id="export">↓ Export state JSON</button><button id="import">↑ Import state JSON</button><button id="reset">Reset</button><button id="observation">Reported observation preset</button><input id="file" type="file" accept="application/json" hidden></div><small>JSON restores optical inputs. Educational selection is included as reference metadata; it does not change the physical solver.</small><p id="notice" role="status"></p></div><div class="evidence" id="evidence"><div class="sectionhead">05 / EVIDENCE & PROVENANCE</div><details open><summary>Computationally verified</summary><p>Geometric ray–plane intersections; shared aperture/material geometry for panel and shadow; 45° / 30° / 60° controls; 97-character transcript and indices; JSON roundtrip; historical DST; solar benchmarks within 0.3°.</p></details><details open><summary>Assumed & approximate</summary><p>Full-screen mode includes both curved text regions, the surrounding cipher, a reverse-reading tableau, an assumed mid-height seam and an approximate tree at the cipher outer end. Two sine lobes, total chord span, heading, clearance and tree size remain hypotheses. CIA describes an 8 ft screen; an NSA summary says about 10 ft. These are competing documentary scenarios, not surveyed certainty. The isolated K4 control omits surrounding text and substitutes 27 blank copper cells for K3. Full-screen glyphs use equal physical stroke cells and approximate counter bridges; they are original generic shapes, not traced serifed hand-cut lettering. Physical pitch is assumed. Copper can be an ideal sheet or a normal-offset solid with aperture walls using separately reported ¼-inch and ½-inch scenarios. Finite uniform solar-disk sampling and tilted/bounded receiver patches are optional numerical experiments. Their preview convergence is not measured site accuracy. Refraction, limb darkening, self-shadow intensity on copper, pools, granite, fasteners, terrain, buildings and photo calibration are omitted. K2 coordinates are a reference location, not a survey.</p></details><details><summary>How to read this experiment</summary><p>Copper blocks sunlight: the dark ground silhouette is the union of its material shadows. The missing copper makes bright letters inside it. Light direction controls ground displacement; incidence depends on each curved surface normal. Camera angle only changes your view. Back views naturally mirror the openings. A projected center marker does not guarantee an unoccluded bright letter.</p><p>The ciphertext is intended to be read from the front; the alphabet tableau is intentionally oriented to be read from the back (CIA description). Both are through-cut apertures, not printed decals. Moving behind the screen mirrors glyph shapes and the spatial order within a row. That is distinct from reversing the canonical 97-letter K4 sequence or changing a geographic bearing by 180°. The entrance compass is a separate installation.</p></details><details><summary>Unsupported observations & source record</summary><p id="obs">Reported OBKR / NGKSSO / NFBNYP / AUEKCAR groupings are unverified user observations. The preset selects those letters only; it does not tune geometry or assert a match. This simulator preserves ciphertext and makes no decoding claim.</p><p><a href="https://www.cia.gov/legacy/headquarters/kryptos-sculpture/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CIA · sculpture, copper & transcript</a><br><a href="https://www.elonka.com/kryptos/transcript.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Elonka Dunin · cross-checked transcript</a><br><a href="https://elonka.com/kryptos/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Dunin · photographs & light context</a><br><a href="https://www.cia.gov/readingroom/docs/kryptos%20sculpture%5B15267759%5D.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CIA released Intellipedia · 8 ft screen description</a><br><a href="https://www.nsa.gov/portals/75/documents/news-features/declassified-documents/cia-kryptos-sculpture/KRYPTOS_Summary.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NSA summary · about 3 m / 10 ft description (p. 2)</a><br><a href="https://jimsanborn.net/content.html#PUBLIC_SPACES" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sanborn · overall installation envelope, not panel dimensions</a><br><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Art_made_of_%22code%22_named_Kryptos_sits_on_the_grounds_of_the_C.I.A._Headquarters_in_Virginia_LCCN2011631531.tif" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Highsmith / Library of Congress · held-out optical reference (not fitted)</a><br><a href="https://voynich.net/Kryptos/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Gillogly · independent viewpoints, unverified capture times</a><br><a href="https://gml.noaa.gov/grad/solcalc/calcdetails.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NOAA · solar calculation method</a></p></details></div></section><section class="evidence" style="margin:2rem 0"><div class="sectionhead">06 / IMAGE-SPACE EVIDENCE WORKSPACE</div><p>Source-pixel observations, not surveyed geometry. Loading evidence does not alter the screen or assign physical scale. Photographs are linked, never redistributed. Partial rubbing coverage does not make the whole screen measured.</p><div class="actions"><button id="loadBoundary">Load 44 boundary picks</button><button id="loadRubbing">Load partial rubbing record</button><button id="importEvidence">Import observation JSON</button><input id="evidenceFile" type="file" accept="application/json" hidden></div><p id="evidenceStatus" role="status">No evidence loaded. State exports preserve loaded observation records and provenance.</p><canvas id="evidenceCanvas" width="768" height="500" style="width:100%;max-height:500px;object-fit:contain;background:#182b22" aria-label="Derived source-pixel landmarks only; source photograph excluded"></canvas><p id="traceLabel"></p><canvas id="traceCanvas" width="649" height="500" style="width:100%;max-height:500px;object-fit:contain;background:#182b22" aria-label="Partial uncalibrated rubbing contour; separate source frame" hidden></canvas><pre id="evidenceDetails" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></section><section class="evidence" style="margin:2rem 0"><div class="sectionhead">07 / CONDITIONAL PHOTO CONSTRAINTS</div><p><strong>Visible strip only · H=1 is dimensionless.</strong> This is a conditional pinhole-camera family, not a surveyed whole panel. 21 non-K4 glyph correspondences: 14 training, 7 held out during camera optimization. Those held-out points were subsequently inspected for exploratory model selection; they are <strong>not untouched final validation</strong>. Highsmith remains unused. Original photographs are excluded.</p><button id="loadPhoto">Load verified conditional photo evidence</button><p id="photoStatus" role="status"></p><label>First-camera focal assumption<select id="photoCase"><option>400</option><option>600</option><option>800</option><option>1200</option><option>2000</option><option>4000</option></select></label><label>Inspect non-K4 glyph<select id="photoFeature"></select></label><label>Strip view yaw · radians<input id="photoYaw" type="range" min="-3.14159" max="3.14159" step="0.02"></label><label>Strip view elevation · radians<input id="photoPitch" type="range" min="0.05" max="1.5" step="0.02"></label><label>Residual-vector magnification<select id="photoResidualScale"><option>1</option><option>10</option><option>20</option></select></label><p>No metric scale, bearing, date or unobserved screen extension is assigned. Selecting a case affects this evidence preview only. Its silhouette endpoints are not verified joins. Sparse glyph points are conditional positions, not traced apertures.</p><canvas id="photoProfiles" width="820" height="270" style="width:100%;background:#182b22" aria-label="Comparison of dimensionless visible-strip profiles"></canvas><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem"><canvas id="photoStrip" width="620" height="500" style="width:min(100%,620px);background:#182b22" aria-label="Conditional three dimensional strip with sparse training and held-out points"></canvas><canvas id="photoResiduals" width="660" height="500" style="width:min(100%,660px);background:#182b22" aria-label="Second-source image coordinates and magnified reprojection residual vectors"></canvas></div><p id="photoPoint" class="mono"></p><div style="overflow-x:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>f₁ assumed px</th><th>f₂ fit px</th><th>Train RMS px</th><th>Held-out RMS px</th><th>Held-out max px</th><th>Length/H</th><th>Sagitta/H</th><th>Exploratory interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody id="photoRows"></tbody></table></div><p id="photoDiagnostics"></p><p>800/1200px scenarios remain nonunique; 4000px has a poor cross-view fit and reaches the second-camera focal bound. Manual bounding-box centers have unquantified systematic errors. <a href="evidence/photo/CALIBRATION_REPORT.md">Full report</a> · <a href="evidence/photo/IMPORT_NOTES.md">Import limits</a> · <a href="https://voynich.net/Kryptos/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Original sources</a></p></section><footer>AN ORIGINAL EXPERIMENTAL WORKBENCH · NOT A SURVEYED RECONSTRUCTION</footer></main><script type="module" src="app.mjs?rev=20261023-fold-1"></script></body></html>
